# /etc/ssh_keys — per-user authorized public keys for AdventOS sshd.
#
# One line per key:
#   <user> ssh-ed25519 <base64-blob> [comment]
#
# The blob is the OpenSSH-format ed25519 public key. Generate one with:
#
#   ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -f mykey
#
# then paste the contents of `mykey.pub` here, with `<user>` prefixed.
# For example, to let `guest` log in with the key in mykey.pub:
#
#   guest ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAI... your-comment-here
#
# Once added (and AdventOS rebuilt), `ssh -i mykey -p 2222 guest@host`
# authenticates over RFC 4252 §7 with no password prompt.
#
# Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored.
#
# sshd ALSO has a built-in demo pubkey for `guest`, matched by
# ssh.elf's `@key` mode (see user/ssh.c DEMO_USER_SEED). That demo
# does not require any entry here.
